# Section 1
privacy-s1-h2 = 1. Introduction & Who We Are
privacy-s1-p2 = located at Rotterdam, The Netherlands, is the <strong>Data Controller</strong> responsible for the processing of your personal data under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).
privacy-s1-p3 = Our commitment is to protect your privacy and handle your data responsibly and transparently. Our primary goals in processing personal information include:
privacy-s1-li2 = Managing your user account (which may include authentication via Google OAuth2), processing payments (if applicable), and providing customer support.
privacy-s1-li3 = Improving and personalizing the Service, including enhancing our AI models (often using anonymized or aggregated data).
privacy-s1-li4 = Ensuring the security and integrity of our Service.
privacy-s1-li5 = Complying with legal obligations, including those related to data accessed via Google APIs, and communicating with you about the Service.
privacy-s1-p4 = We adhere to GDPR, the Google API Services User Data Policy (see Section 14), and other relevant regulations to protect your data against unauthorized access, disclosure, alteration, and destruction.

# Section 2
privacy-s2-h2 = 2. Scope of this Policy

# Section 3
privacy-s3-h2 = 3. Information We Collect
privacy-s3-1-h3 = 3.1. Information You Provide Directly
privacy-s3-1-li1 = <strong>Account Information:</strong> When you register, we collect information such as your name, email address, and password. If you register or log in using Google OAuth2, we will collect information as described in Section 3.4.
privacy-s3-1-li2 = <strong>Payment Information:</strong> If you subscribe to paid features, we (or our third-party payment processor) collect billing details like your name, address, and payment card information. We do not store your full payment card details ourselves.
privacy-s3-1-li4 = <strong>Communications:</strong> If you contact us for support or feedback, we collect the information contained in your communications (e.g., email content, support ticket details).
privacy-s3-2-h3 = 3.2. Information Collected Automatically
privacy-s3-2-li1 = <strong>Usage Data:</strong> Information about how you interact with the Service, such as features used, content generated, time spent, clicks, settings preferences, and error logs.
privacy-s3-2-li2 = <strong>Device and Connection Information:</strong> Technical data including your IP address, browser type and version, operating system, device identifiers (where applicable), and general location derived from your IP address.
privacy-s3-2-li3 = <strong>Cookies and Tracking Technologies:</strong> We use cookies and similar technologies to operate the Service, understand usage, and for analytics. See Section 9 ("Cookies") for details.
privacy-s3-4-h3 = 3.4. Information Received via Google OAuth2 (If Applicable)
privacy-s3-4-p1 = If you choose to connect your Google account to our Service using OAuth2 (e.g., for signing in or accessing Google services like Google Drive), we will collect and process information from Google based on the permissions you grant. This may include:
privacy-s3-4-li2-title = <strong>If you connect Google Drive:</strong>
privacy-s3-4-li2-sub1 = To allow you to use files from your Google Drive as input, we may access the names, identifiers, and content of specific files you explicitly select within our application. This access is typically read-only for the selected files.
privacy-s3-4-li2-sub2 = To allow you to save generated content to your Google Drive, we may require permission to create new files in a location you specify within your Google Drive.
privacy-s3-4-li3 = The specific data accessed and the permissions requested will be clearly presented to you during the Google OAuth2 consent process. We only access data that is necessary for the functionality you choose to use.
privacy-s3-4-p2 = Our use of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the Google API Services User Data Policy, including the Limited Use requirements (see Section 14).

# Section 4
privacy-s4-h2 = 4. How We Use Your Information & Legal Basis (GDPR)
privacy-s4-p1 = We process your personal data based on specific legal grounds under GDPR:
privacy-s4-li1-title = <strong>To Provide and Manage the Service (Legal Basis: Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR - Performance of Contract):</strong>
privacy-s4-li1-sub1 = Creating and managing your user account, including authentication using credentials you create or via Google OAuth2.
privacy-s4-li1-sub2 = Processing your input data (including any data accessed via Google APIs with your consent) to generate requested AI content (images, videos).
privacy-s4-li1-sub3 = Delivering the generated content to you.
privacy-s4-li1-sub4 = Processing payments and managing subscriptions.
privacy-s4-li1-sub5 = Providing customer support and responding to inquiries.
privacy-s4-li1-sub6-title = <strong>How we use Google data accessed via OAuth2:</strong>
privacy-s4-li1-sub6-ss2 = Pre-fill your account details (name and email) within our Service.
privacy-s4-li2-title = <strong>To Improve and Develop the Service (Legal Basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR - Legitimate Interests):</strong>
privacy-s4-li2-sub1 = Analyzing usage patterns to understand user needs and enhance features (Usage Data).
privacy-s4-li2-sub2 = Improving the performance, accuracy, and safety of our AI models. This may involve analyzing Input Data (including data accessed via Google APIs if used for model training, which requires explicit disclosure and compliance with Limited Use) and Generated Content, typically in an anonymized or aggregated form where feasible. Our legitimate interest is in providing a better, safer, and more effective Service.
privacy-s4-li2-sub3 = Troubleshooting and debugging issues.
privacy-s4-li3-title = <strong>For Security and Compliance (Legal Basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR - Legitimate Interests; Art. 6(1)(c) GDPR - Legal Obligation):</strong>
privacy-s4-li3-sub1 = Protecting the security and integrity of our Service, preventing fraud and abuse (Usage Data, Device Info).
privacy-s4-li3-sub2 = Complying with applicable laws, regulations, and legal processes, including requirements from Google regarding API usage.
privacy-s4-li4-title = <strong>For Communication & Marketing (Legal Basis: Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR - Consent; Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR - Legitimate Interests):</strong>
privacy-s4-li4-sub1 = Sending important service-related communications (e.g., account updates, security alerts) (Legitimate Interest/Contract).
privacy-s4-li4-sub2 = Sending promotional communications or newsletters *if* you have opted-in (Consent). You can opt-out at any time.

# Section 5
privacy-s5-h2 = 5. Data Sharing and Disclosure
privacy-s5-p1 = We do not sell your personal data. We may share your information in the following limited circumstances:
privacy-s5-1-h3 = 5.1. Third-Party Service Providers (Subprocessors)
privacy-s5-1-p1 = We engage trusted third-party companies and individuals to perform services on our behalf (e.g., payment processing, data hosting, analytics, security, customer support, AI infrastructure). These subprocessors only have access to the personal data necessary to perform their tasks and are contractually obligated (via Data Processing Agreements - DPAs where required by GDPR) to protect your data and use it solely for the purposes we specify.
privacy-s5-1-p2 = Key categories of subprocessors may include:
