privacy-s5-2-h3 = 5.2. Legal Requirements
privacy-s5-2-p1 = We may disclose your information if required by law, subpoena, or other legal process, or if we have a good faith belief that disclosure is necessary to protect our rights, protect your safety or the safety of others, investigate fraud, or respond to a government request.
privacy-s5-3-h3 = 5.3. Business Transfers
privacy-s5-4-h3 = 5.4. Handling of Google User Data
privacy-s5-4-li2 = We will not transfer this Google-sourced basic profile information to others unless doing so is necessary to provide and improve these authentication and account management features (e.g., to our backend service providers strictly for these purposes, under confidentiality obligations), to comply with applicable law, or as part of a merger, acquisition, or sale of assets (with notice to you).
privacy-s5-4-li3 = The App will not use this Google-sourced basic profile information for serving advertisements.
privacy-s5-4-li4-title = The App will not allow humans to read this Google-sourced basic profile information unless:
privacy-s5-4-li4-sub1 = We have your affirmative agreement for a specific, legitimate purpose (e.g., assisting with an account issue you reported).
privacy-s5-4-li4-sub2 = Doing so is necessary for security purposes such as investigating abuse.
privacy-s5-4-li4-sub3 = To comply with applicable law.
privacy-s5-4-li4-sub4 = For the App's internal operations (e.g., customer support, troubleshooting) related to your account, and even then only when the data is directly relevant to the operation and access is limited and logged.
privacy-s5-4-li5 = Our use and transfer of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the Google API Services User Data Policy, including the Limited Use requirements (see Section 14 for more details).

# Section 6
privacy-s6-h2 = 6. International Data Transfers
privacy-s6-p1 = Your personal information may be transferred to, and processed in, countries other than the country in which you reside. These countries may have data protection laws that are different from the laws of your country (particularly if you are in the EU/EEA).
privacy-s6-p2 = Specifically, some of our third-party service providers (as listed in Section 5) may be located outside the European Economic Area (EEA), for example, in the United States.
privacy-s6-p3 = Where we transfer your personal data outside the EEA, we take appropriate safeguards to ensure your data receives an adequate level of protection. This typically includes relying on:
privacy-s6-li1 = An adequacy decision by the European Commission confirming the country provides adequate protection.
privacy-s6-li2 = Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs) approved by the European Commission, implemented between us and the third-party provider.
privacy-s6-li3 = For transfers to the U.S., we may rely on providers certified under the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework (or its successor) or utilize SCCs.

# Section 7
privacy-s7-h2 = 7. Data Storage and Protection
privacy-s7-h3 = Data Security Measures:
privacy-s7-p1 = We implement appropriate technical and organizational security measures designed to protect your personal data, including any data accessed via Google APIs, against accidental or unlawful destruction, loss, alteration, unauthorized disclosure, or access. These measures include:
privacy-s7-li1-title = Encryption
privacy-s7-li1-text = : Using encryption (e.g., TLS/SSL) for data in transit and encryption for sensitive data at rest.
privacy-s7-li2-title = Access Control
privacy-s7-li2-text = : Limiting access to personal data to authorized personnel with a legitimate need to know, based on roles and responsibilities, and in accordance with policies such as Google's Limited Use requirements.
privacy-s7-li3-title = Security Audits and Monitoring
privacy-s7-li3-text = : Regularly reviewing our security practices and monitoring systems for potential vulnerabilities and attacks.
privacy-s7-li4-title = Secure Development Practices:
privacy-s7-li4-text = Incorporating security considerations into our software development lifecycle.
privacy-s7-p2 = However, please note that no method of transmission over the Internet or electronic storage is 100% secure. While we strive to use commercially acceptable means to protect your personal data, we cannot guarantee its absolute security.

# Section 8
privacy-s8-h2 = 8. Data Retention
privacy-s8-p1 = We retain your personal data only for as long as necessary to fulfill the purposes for which we collected it, including for the purposes of satisfying any legal, accounting, or reporting requirements, and for providing and improving the Service.
privacy-s8-p2 = To determine the appropriate retention period, we consider:
privacy-s8-li1 = The amount, nature, and sensitivity of the personal data.
privacy-s8-li2 = The potential risk of harm from unauthorized use or disclosure.
privacy-s8-li3 = The purposes for which we process the data (including the purpose of authentication using Google basic profile information if you choose to use Google Sign-In) and whether we can achieve those purposes through other means.
privacy-s8-li4 = Applicable legal requirements (e.g., financial record retention periods) and any specific retention requirements from services like Google for basic profile data accessed via their APIs for authentication.
privacy-s8-p3 = Generally:
privacy-s8-li5-title = <strong>Account Information (including Google-derived basic profile data such as your email, name, and profile picture, if you sign in with Google):</strong>
privacy-s8-li6-title = <strong>Input Data (provided directly by you for AI generation) & Generated Output:</strong>
privacy-s8-li7-title = <strong>Usage Data:</strong>
privacy-s8-li7-text = Often retained for a specific period (e.g., 12-24 months) for analysis to improve our Service, and then may be aggregated or deleted.
privacy-s8-li8-title = <strong>Billing Information (if applicable):</strong>
privacy-s8-li8-text = Retained according to legal requirements for financial records.
privacy-s8-p4 = You can request the deletion of your account and associated personal data, including any basic profile data retrieved from Google services for authentication, subject to the rights outlined in Section 10. We will also delete your Google user data (email, name, profile picture used for authentication) upon your request to delete your account, or if it's no longer needed for the stated purpose of account management and authentication.

# Section 9
privacy-s9-h2 = 9. Cookies and Tracking Technologies
privacy-s9-h3 = Types of Cookies We Use:
privacy-s9-li1 = <strong>Strictly Necessary Cookies:</strong> Essential for the operation of the Service (e.g., authentication, security, session management). These cannot be disabled. (Legal Basis: Contract/Legitimate Interest).
privacy-s9-li2 = <strong>Performance and Analytics Cookies:</strong> Help us understand how users interact with the Service, measure performance, and identify areas for improvement (e.g., Google Analytics). (Legal Basis: Consent, or Legitimate Interest with safeguards).
privacy-s9-li3 = <strong>Functional Cookies:</strong> Enable enhanced functionality and personalization (e.g., remembering preferences). (Legal Basis: Consent).
privacy-s9-li4 = <strong>Advertising and Targeting Cookies:</strong> Used by us or third parties (like Meta) to deliver relevant advertising, measure campaign effectiveness, and track users across websites (if applicable). (Legal Basis: Consent).
privacy-s9-2-h3 = Your Choices and Consent:
privacy-s9-2-p1 = When you first visit our website or use the app where non-essential cookies are used, we will request your consent via a cookie banner or similar mechanism. You can manage your preferences and withdraw consent at any time through our cookie settings tool or your browser settings.
privacy-s9-2-p2-prefix = For more detailed information about the specific cookies we use, their purposes, and how to manage them, please see our separate
privacy-s9-2-p2-link-text = Cookie Policy

# Section 10
privacy-s10-h2 = 10. Your Data Protection Rights (GDPR)
privacy-s10-p1 = If you are located in the European Economic Area (EEA) or UK, you have the following rights regarding your personal data:
privacy-s10-li1 = <strong>Right of Access (Article 15 GDPR):</strong> To request access to the personal information we hold about you, including any data obtained from Google.
privacy-s10-li2 = <strong>Right to Rectification (Article 16 GDPR):</strong> To request correction of inaccurate or incomplete data.
privacy-s10-li3 = <strong>Right to Erasure ('Right to be Forgotten') (Article 17 GDPR):</strong> To request deletion of your personal data under certain conditions. This includes data obtained via Google OAuth2.
privacy-s10-li4 = <strong>Right to Restriction of Processing (Article 18 GDPR):</strong> To request restriction of processing under certain conditions.
privacy-s10-li5 = <strong>Right to Data Portability (Article 20 GDPR):</strong> To receive your data in a machine-readable format and transmit it to another controller.
privacy-s10-li6 = <strong>Right to Object (Article 21 GDPR):</strong> To object to processing based on legitimate interests or for direct marketing.
privacy-s10-li7 = <strong>Right to Withdraw Consent (Article 7(3) GDPR):</strong> To withdraw consent at any time where processing is based on consent (including consent for accessing Google data), without affecting prior lawful processing. You can also typically manage or revoke Google's access to your data via your Google Account security settings page.
privacy-s10-li8 = <strong>Right to Lodge a Complaint (Article 77 GDPR):</strong> To lodge a complaint with your local supervisory authority (Data Protection Authority) if you believe our processing infringes GDPR.
privacy-s10-h3 = Exercising Your Rights:
privacy-s10-p2 = To exercise these rights, including requesting deletion of your data (including Google-sourced data), please contact us using the details in Section 1 ("Introduction & Who We Are") or Section 13 ("Contact Us"). We will respond within the timeframes required by GDPR (typically one month), potentially after verifying your identity.

